  ('csa-u4-q15', 'ap_csa', '4.9', '4', 'P1', 'mcq', 'You want to remove every `0` from an `ArrayList<Integer>`. Which loop design is **correct** (no skipped elements, no exception)?', '{"A":"Enhanced-for: `for (int x : list) if (x == 0) list.remove(...);`","B":"Forward loop with `i++` always: removing at `i` then `i++`","C":"Backward index loop: `for (int i = list.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (list.get(i) == 0) list.remove(i);`","D":"for (int i = 0; i < list.size(); i++) list.remove(i);"}', 'C', NULL, 'Iterating **backward** means a left-shift after `remove` never skips an unexamined element. (A) throws `ConcurrentModificationException`; (B) skips the shifted-in element; (D) removes the wrong elements as the list shrinks.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
  ('csa-u4-q16', 'ap_csa', '4.10', '4', 'P3', 'mcq', 'What does `list` contain after this runs?
